SESSION STARTS
   |
   |-- TRANSACTION STARTS
   |      |
   |      |-- INSERT
   |      |-- UPDATE
   |      |
   |      |-- COMMIT  ---> permanent
   |      |-- ROLLBACK ---> nothing happened
   |
SESSION CONTINUES (can start another transaction)


a client connects to the database ---ie is a session{authentication ,var initiazled etc
}
Session begins

A database session is created
Authentication, variables, context are set
No transaction yet (or an implicit one, depending on DB)

BEGIN TRANSACTION;
or call procedure that starts a transaction
A transaction starts
The transaction lives inside the session
All changes are temporary

transaction executes 2 sql stmnst like insert, update, delete
INSERT INTO orders VALUES (101, 'CREATED');
Row is inserted
Row is not yet permanent
Other sessions cannot see it
Locks are held

the transaction executes another sql stmnt
UPDATE orders SET status = 'CONFIRMED' WHERE order_id = 101;

still same -- nothing is permanent

COMMIT --> this step release the lock ,other sessions can see and the data is permannently saved

if failure -- rollback --> all changes are undone ,nothing is saved

=================================================
NOw if a transaction has commit inside it
CREATE PROCEDURE create_order_bad(p_order_id INT)
AS
BEGIN
    INSERT INTO orders VALUES (p_order_id, 'CREATED');
    COMMIT;

    UPDATE orders
    SET status = 'CONFIRMED'
    WHERE order_id = p_order_id;
END;

CALL create_order_bad(101); this proc bascialyy has to insert and update status
Step by step:

INSERT runs
COMMIT happens
Transaction ends
Row is permanent
UPDATE fails
Caller tries ROLLBACK

❌ Rollback does NOTHING
Because the transaction already ended.

One-Line Final Mental Model

Session holds the conversation
Transaction holds the promise
Procedure does the work
Commit keeps the promise
Rollback pretends nothing happened



SESSION ENDS
   |
   |-- All transactions must be ended (committed or rolled back)
   |-- Connection to database is closed
   |-- Session context is destroyed
